{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf filter [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [--gene GENE] [--genes GENES]\n                             [--gene-file FILE] [--preset NAME] [--bed FILE] [--pad-kb PAD_KB]\n                             [-r REGION] [--expr EXPR] [--exclude-near-gaps]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Input VCF file path.\n  --gene GENE           Keep a gene by symbol (repeatable).\n  --genes GENES         Comma-separated gene symbols (repeatable).\n  --gene-file FILE      File of gene symbols (whitespace or comma-separated; # starts a comment).\n  --preset NAME         Gene panel preset (repeatable): pharmacogenes, hla, autoimmune, acmg-sf,\n                        cardiac\n  --bed FILE            BED or BED.gz panel, unioned with the selected gene spans.\n  --pad-kb PAD_KB       Padding on each side of a gene span, in kb (default: 0).\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region(s); when a panel is given, restrict its union to these\n                        regions.\n  --expr EXPR           bcftools filter expression (e.g. 'QUAL>30')\n  --exclude-near-gaps   Exclude variants in or near genomic gaps (requires Count Ns output)\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf filter --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --genes BRCA1,BRCA2 --bed targets.bed\n  wgsextract vcf filter --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --expr 'QUAL>30'\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  filtered.vcf.gz (+ .tbi).\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: bgzip, samtools;\n  minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
